        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "How are you feeling generally lately?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "I am tired, even after sleeping a lot. I just wake up feeling heavy, like I am carrying a weight around that I cannot explain."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Are you experiencing any change in appetite?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Not really. I eat when I have to, but it is not satisfying. I just feel like I am going through the motions of eating, without really tasting anything."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "When you are tired even after sleeping a lot. How is your energy level in general?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "It is pretty low. I can't even walk the stairs without getting winded. I feel like I am losing my strength, like my body is just giving in."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Do you also have experienced any changes in your sleeping pattern, like going to bed to completly different times?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes, I am not sleeping at the right hours. I lie down at three in the morning and stare at the ceiling, thinking about things I cannot control."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "The things that you cannot control. What specific thoughts do you have?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Just worries about the future. My mum is getting older, and I am worried that I am not doing enough to help her."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "These worries and that you are not doing enough, How does that make you feel?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Guilty. I feel like I should be doing more to help her, but I am just so tired all the time that I don't know what to do."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "How does that guilt change your attitude towards yourself?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "It makes me feel like I am failing. I am not the person I used to be, and I don't know how to get back to that."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "When you say you are failing. Do you have at any time the urge to punish yourself for it?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Sometimes. I look at my mum and I think, 'Why can't I be stronger for her?' I know that is not fair, but it feels like the truth."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "What are things that you have tried to be \"stronger\"?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "I've tried to push through the fatigue, but I just end up collapsing. I have tried to cook for her, but I just burn the food."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "When you say that you burn the food. Do you have difficulties concentrating on for example cooking?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes, my mind wanders. I start to chop vegetables and then I realize I have no idea what I am making."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Is cooking something that you find fun?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Not anymore. I used to love it, but now it just feels like a chore. I look at the recipe and I just stare at it, unable to remember the next step."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "In the example with cooking. Do you find it hard to decide what to do? What recipe you want to cook?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "I stand in front of the fridge for ages, trying to decide what to make, and I just end up making nothing because I cannot decide."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "In the moments were you cannot decide and were you feel you are not strong enough for others. How does that make you feel about yourself?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "It makes me feel weak. I look at my mum and I think, 'Why can't I be the person she needs?' I know I am not doing enough, and it makes me feel like I am failing her."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Did you have at any time the feeling that you are not worth?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes. I lie there at night thinking that maybe I am not worth her love because I am not doing enough to help her."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "At those moments did you had at any moment the urge to harm yourself?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "No, I never wanted to hurt myself. I just feel empty."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "So I want to ask directly. Did you ever thought of suicide?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes. It crosses my mind sometimes. I think about how much easier it would be if I just went away, but I know that would hurt her too much."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "When for example you are thinking about how it would hurt her, do you sometimes cry in such moments?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes. I cry a lot. I cry because I am so sorry that I am not the person she deserves."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "On a scale from 1-10. How sad did you feel in the last two weeks in general?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "I would say it is a 10. I feel like I have lost myself completely."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Do you sense any hope that it will get better in the next weeks?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Not really. I think about the future, and I just don't see a way out."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "You said that you now view cooking only as a chore, but it was something you enjoyed. Is there any other hobby that you lost interest in?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes, reading. I used to love reading, but lately, I just can't focus on a book. I pick it up and I just stare at the page, and I have to put it down because I can't keep my mind on it."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Are there moments when you feel irritable because of your situation?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Yes, all the time. I am just so tired and frustrated that I feel like I am snapping at everyone."
        },
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Are you in a relationsship? And how do you show the irritability there?"
        },
        {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "I am married. I am just so short-tempered. I shout at him for things he didn't even do."
        },
        {
